<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imperator Romanorum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Emperor of the Romans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imperator Romanorum, meaning Emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, was the imperial title revived in the West when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> was crowned by the pope in 800. It claimed continuity with the Roman Empire. It was a founding element of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>'s ideology and was later taken up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperors</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imperator-romanorum.jpg" alt="Imperator Romanorum" width="276" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hans_Burgkmair_d._%C3%84._005.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
